{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"diagnosis\":\"The nil case simplified away the three-factor shape required by `timeOrderF_timeOrderF_mid`; reintroducing a trailing unit lets that theorem time-order `b` before applying the equal-time supercommutator lemma. In the successor case, `ofCrAnListF [χ]` was not normalized to `ofCrAnOpF χ`, so the induction hypothesis and vanishing nested-supercommutator equation could not match the goal associatively.\",\"proof_body\":\"by\\n  classical\\n  let p (a : 𝓕.FieldOpFreeAlgebra)\\n      (ha : a ∈ Submodule.span ℂ (Set.range ofCrAnListFBasis)) : Prop :=\\n    ι 𝓣ᶠ(a * [ofCrAnOpF φ, ofCrAnOpF ψ]ₛF * b) =\\n      ι ([ofCrAnOpF φ, ofCrAnOpF ψ]ₛF * 𝓣ᶠ(a * b))\\n  change p a (Basis.mem_span _ a)\\n  apply Submodule.span_induction\\n  · rintro x ⟨φs, rfl⟩\\n    simp only [ofListBasis_eq_ofList, p]\\n    revert b\\n    induction φs using List.reverseRecOn with\\n    | nil =>\\n        intro b\\n        simp only [ofCrAnListF_nil, one_mul]\\n        rw [← mul_one ([ofCrAnOpF φ, ofCrAnOpF ψ]ₛF * b)]\\n        rw [timeOrderF_timeOrderF_mid]\\n        simp only [mul_one]\\n        rw [timeOrderF_superCommuteF_ofCrAnOpF_ofCrAnOpF_eq_time hφψ hψφ]\\n    | append_singleton φs χ ih =>\\n        intro b\\n        have hn := ι_timeOrderF_superCommuteF_superCommuteF\\n          (φ1 := χ) (φ2 := φ) (φ3 := ψ) (ofCrAnListF φs) b\\n        have hi := ih (ofCrAnOpF χ * b)\\n        by_cases hs : 𝓕.crAnStatistics φ = 𝓕.crAnStatistics ψ\\n        · simp_all [ofCrAnListF_append, ofCrAnListF_singleton, superCommuteF,\\n            mul_assoc, mul_add, add_mul]\\n        · simp_all [ofCrAnListF_append, ofCrAnListF_singleton, superCommuteF,\\n            mul_assoc, mul_add, add_mul, map_mul, ι_superCommuteF_of_diff_statistic hs]\\n  · simp [p]\\n  · intro x y hx hy hpx hpy\\n    simp_all [p, add_mul, mul_add]\\n  · intro x hx hpx\\n    simp_all [p]\"}"}}
